    snapraidd.conf.example     example of the new option
    README                     note about the fork


How it is tested
----------------

A Docker lab with emulated disks, and the tests of the API against real
filesystems, are in a separate repository:

    https://github.com/paleka/snapraid-lab

The screenshots of the Storage page are there too. No picture is added to
this repository, to keep the difference from the original project small.


Keeping up with the original project
------------------------------------

    git remote add upstream https://github.com/amadvance/snapraid-daemon.git
    git fetch upstream
    git checkout master && git merge --ff-only upstream/master
    git checkout storage && git rebase master
